hypotheses.statement:
With the notation of Proposition <a href="#prop:isolation" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:isolation">6</a>, there is a projective crepant $\mathbb Q$-factorial dlt modification $$f:(Y_d,\Sigma)\longrightarrow (Y,S_Y)$$ such that $\Sigma$ is reduced, $$\label{eq:dlt-support}
  \operatorname{Supp}\Sigma=\operatorname{Supp}f^*S_Y,$$ and $f$ is an isomorphism off $S_Y$. On a neighborhood of $\Sigma$, $$\label{eq:dlt-local}
  K_{Y_d}+\Sigma\sim_{\mathbb Q}\tau s f^*S_Y.$$ Moreover, $f^*S_Y$ is numerically trivial on each component of $\Sigma$, and $Y_d$ shares the open $U_X$ with $X$ and $Y$.

